# Excel/Office temporary lock files
~$*

# Explorer leaves these behind when it records a folder's view state or builds
# thumbnails. Both are Hidden and System, so they are invisible in Explorer
# unless protected operating system files are shown, and in PowerShell without
# -Force - but git sees them like any other file.
desktop.ini
Thumbs.db

# Raw captures of the console output that appears in README.md. The README
# carries the text itself - Markdown has no include mechanism, so a file here
# could only ever be a second copy of it, free to drift. docs/images is
# tracked: a picture the README points at has to be in the repository.
docs/text/

# Archive. Not published, and not version controlled at all: these files do not
# change, and the backup chain already covers them. Git is here for history and
# bisect, neither of which means anything for dead files.
Old/

# Prod/ and Work/ are tracked as folders but their contents are not - see the
# .gitignore inside each. The rules live there rather than here so that the
# folders' own .gitignore and README.md stay trackable.
